From: =?UTF-8?q?Witold=20Bo=C5=82t?= <witold.bolt@jit.team>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:00:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] broadcom/compiler: propagate defin/defout in program order

vir_live_variables_defin_defout_dataflow() spreads each block's (partial)
definitions to its successors, a forward problem, but visited the blocks
in reverse order: a definition moved one block per pass, so the loop ran
about as many passes as the program has blocks in a row, each pass over
all blocks and all temps. Liveness is recomputed after every spill, and
for a big shader (an unrolled WGSL loop: 667 blocks, 10.5k temps, 13k
instructions) this pass was 225 ms of each of the 81 recomputations its
register allocation went through, most of a 33 s compile.

Visit the blocks in program order; the fixpoint is the same (the union
of the definitions reaching each block), it is reached in a couple of
passes for acyclic code.

Raspberry Pi 4 (V3D 4.2), the compositor pipelines of a wgpu/Vulkan
application with the shader cache disabled: its largest fragment shader
27.5 -> 9.9 s (measured with the next commit's liveness changes
applied), the same QPU code for all 105 shaders of the set
(V3D_DEBUG=qpu,fs,vs,cs output equal), shader-db stats equal.

Ported unchanged from a Mesa 26.2.x tree used by another operating
system port on the same board (Raspberry Pi 4, V3D 4.2). The numbers
below were measured there, not yet on Phoenix-RTOS.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/broadcom/compiler/vir_live_variables.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_live_variables.c b/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_live_variables.c
index 34e2e5f..cb7fd70 100644
--- a/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_live_variables.c
+++ b/src/broadcom/compiler/vir_live_variables.c
@@ -358,7 +358,11 @@ vir_live_variables_defin_defout_dataflow(struct v3d_compile *c, int bitset_words
 {
         bool cont = false;
 
-        vir_for_each_block_rev(block, c) {
+        /* A forward problem: in program order a definition reaches the end
+         * of an acyclic region in one pass (in reverse order it moved one
+         * block per pass, and a big unrolled shader took hundreds of passes).
+         */
+        vir_for_each_block(block, c) {
                 /* Propagate defin/defout down the successors to produce the
                  * union of blocks with a reachable (partial) definition of
                  * the var.
